    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration `set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 1 family ccc`:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n xconnect 3.3.3.3 2 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Cisco command assumes the same L2VPN neighbor (3.3.3.3) and virtual circuit ID (2) as specified in the `protocols l2circuit` configuration.\\n2. The encapsulation type defaults to MPLS in Cisco, which matches the Juniper CCC (Circuit Cross Connect) functionality.\\n3. In Cisco, this would be part of an MPLS L2VPN/VPLS configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'xconnect 3.3.3.3 2 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco IOS command for the Juniper configuration `set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 1 family ccc`:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n xconnect 3.3.3.3 2 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Cisco command assumes the same L2VPN neighbor (3.3.3.3) and virtual circuit ID (2) as specified in the `protocols l2circuit` configuration.\\n2. The encapsulation type defaults to MPLS in Cisco, which matches the Juniper CCC (Circuit Cross Connect) functionality.\\n3. In Cisco, this would be part of an MPLS L2VPN/VPLS configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'xconnect 3.3.3.3 2 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
